---
import PrivacyLayout from "../../components/PrivacyLayout.astro";
---

<PrivacyLayout
    title="Privacy Policy - Dialettario"
    appName="Dialettario"
    lastUpdated="31 agosto 2025"
    accentColor="#6366f1"
>
    <div class="highlight">
        <strong>In summary:</strong> Dialettario is a simple dictionary app that
        works offline. We collect minimal data and display advertising through Google
        AdMob, which may collect data according to their policies.
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
        Dialettario is a mobile application designed to provide dictionary
        functionality and language learning features. The app is developed with
        privacy in mind and operates primarily offline.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Data we do NOT collect ourselves</h2>
    <p>Dialettario does not directly collect, transmit, share, or sell:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Personal dictionary searches or vocabulary data</li>
        <li>Learning progress or study habits</li>
        <li>Personally identifiable information</li>
        <li>Location data</li>
        <li>Device contacts or files</li>
        <li>Biometric data or authentication information</li>
        <li>Language preferences or app settings</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Advertising and Google AdMob</h2>
    <p>To support app development, we use Google AdMob which may collect:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Advertising identifiers (Advertising ID)</li>
        <li>Device information (model, OS version)</li>
        <li>App usage data for advertising purposes</li>
        <li>Network and connection information</li>
        <li>Approximate location data (for geo-targeted ads)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        This data is handled directly by Google according to their
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank"
            >Privacy Policy</a
        >
        and
        <a
            href="https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543"
            target="_blank">AdMob Policies</a
        >.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Dictionary content and offline functionality</h2>
    <p>
        Dialettario includes pre-loaded dictionary content that is stored
        locally on your device. This content includes:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Dictionary definitions and translations</li>
        <li>Example sentences and usage information</li>
        <li>Pronunciation guides (where available)</li>
        <li>Language learning materials</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        All dictionary searches and interactions with this content remain on
        your device and are not transmitted to external servers.
    </p>

    <h2>5. App permissions</h2>
    <p>Dialettario requests minimal permissions:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Internet access:</strong> Required to display advertisements
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Network state:</strong> To check connectivity for ad loading
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Local storage:</strong> To save app preferences and user progress
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        We do not request access to camera, microphone, contacts, location, or
        other sensitive device features.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Data storage and security</h2>
    <p>All app data is stored locally on your device:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Dictionary content:</strong> Pre-loaded and stored locally
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>User preferences:</strong> Stored in local app storage
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Search history:</strong> Kept locally and can be cleared by the
            user
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Favorites/Bookmarks:</strong> Stored locally on the device
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>Dialettario integrates only:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Google AdMob:</strong> For advertising (subject to Google policies)
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        We do not use analytics services, crash reporting, or other third-party
        tracking beyond advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
        Dialettario may be suitable for educational use by children. We do not
        knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. The app's
        offline nature and minimal data collection make it appropriate for
        educational environments.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Advertising controls</h2>
    <p>You can control ad personalization:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Android:</strong> Settings > Google > Ads > Opt out of Ads Personalization
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>iOS:</strong> Settings > Privacy & Security > Apple Advertising
            > Personalized Ads
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>10. Data retention</h2>
    <p>Since most data remains on your device, you control retention by:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Clearing search history within the app</li>
        <li>Resetting app preferences</li>
        <li>Uninstalling the app (removes all local data)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Advertising data retention is governed by Google AdMob policies.</p>

    <h2>11. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>Updates to this privacy policy will be communicated through:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>App store updates</li>
        <li>In-app notifications (if implemented)</li>
        <li>Updated privacy policy publication</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>12. Regulatory compliance</h2>
    <p>Dialettario is designed to comply with:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation)</strong>
        </li>
        <li><strong>CCPA (California Consumer Privacy Act)</strong></li>
        <li>
            <strong>COPPA (Children's Online Privacy Protection Act)</strong>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="highlight">
        <strong>Remember:</strong> Your dictionary searches and learning progress
        never leave your device. Only advertising data is handled by Google AdMob
        according to their policies.
    </div>

    <div slot="additional-contact">
        <p>
            For advertising-related matters, contact
            <a
                href="https://support.google.com/ads/contact/abg_afc"
                target="_blank">Google AdMob Support</a
            > directly.
        </p>
    </div>
</PrivacyLayout>
